OL,3,AMan City not 'above the rules', says No
OL,4,A10 after backlash to Burnham remarks
OL,5,
OL,6,FDowning Street has said Manchester City
OL,7,Fare not "above the rules" after Andy
OL,8,FBurnham was criticised for his comments
OL,9,Fabout the club's breaches of Premier
OL,10,FLeague financial rules.
OL,12,FThe prime minister said on Wednesday he
OL,13,Fwould be "really concerned" if the
OL,14,Fclub's owners decide to sell up after
OL,15,FCity were found guilty by an
OL,16,Findependent commission of most of the
OL,17,F115 charges they faced.
OL,19,FHis remarks were branded "completely
OL,20,Fout of touch" and "extraordinary" by
OL,21,Fthe Tories and took many in the
OL,22,Ffootball community by surprise.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
